# Increase arrset pass/cycle limits in eq3nr110.f to match v8.0a values.
#
# The DEW EQ3 R110 code uses nplim=4 and ncylim=7, which are the original
# 1987 values from the monolithic source.  The upstream v8.0a EQ3NR refactored
# these into arrset.f (line 202) and raised them to nplim=7 / ncylim=15.
#
# nplim  controls the maximum number of passes in the arrset starting-estimate
#        loop.  Each pass refines ionic strength, activity of water, and
#        activity coefficients before re-solving the simultaneous constraint
#        system via arrsim.
# ncylim controls the maximum number of inner cycles within each pass, used
#        to refine species concentrations.
#
# The tighter limits cause arrset to exit with "optimization ended outside
# requested limits" for constraint combinations that require more iterations
# to converge — in particular solid-solution equilibrium (jflag=20) and
# redox-coupled species (jflag=27) under non-ambient conditions.
#
# This change brings the DEW R110 code in line with the current v8.0a standard.
#
# Intended for upstream submission to gitlab.com/ENKI-portal/SUPCRTandEQs.
--- a/upstream-dew/EQ3/eq3nr110.f
+++ b/upstream-dew/EQ3/eq3nr110.f
@@ -1421,7 +1421,7 @@ c   species concentrations before new estimates of ionic strength, etc.,
 c   are made.
 c
-      data nlopmx/12/,nplim/4/,ncylim/7/
+      data nlopmx/12/,nplim/7/,ncylim/15/
       data nttyi/5/
